@startuml credentials-lifecycle
title Credential Lifecycle: Issue, Renew, and Holder Operations

|Credential issuance|
start
:CredentialRegistryFactory_Issue;
:Anchorers and holders authorize initial creation;
:Create one canonical registered credential;
stop

|Intrinsic credential renewal|
start
:Credential implementing CredentialLifecycle
with an existing validUntil;
:CredentialLifecycle_Renew;
:Anchorers authorize renewal;
:Require requested validUntil
strictly later than current validUntil;
:Atomically consume the old contract
and create one replacement;
:Preserve every other credential field;
:Natural expiry after validUntil
requires no transaction;
stop

|Registered credential renewal|
start
:Canonical contract implementing Credential,
CredentialLifecycle, RegisteredCredential,
and RegisteredCredentialLifecycle;
:RegisteredCredentialLifecycle_Renew;
:Anchorers and registry administrator
jointly authorize renewal;
:Require requested time strictly later
than validUntil and expiresAt;
:Set intrinsic validUntil and registration
expiresAt to the same requested time;
:Atomically consume the old contract
and create one replacement;
:Preserve all other credential
and registration fields;
if (Payment required by profile?) then (yes)
  :Apply profile-specific payment authorization;
else (no)
  :No payment required by the generic interface;
endif
stop

|Holder operations|
start
:Canonical Credential with 0..n holders and 1..n anchorers;
if (One holder relinquishes?) then (yes)
  :Credential_RemoveSelfAsHolder;
  :Consume old contract and create one replacement;
  :Remove only the exercising holder, including the final holder;
  :Preserve anchorers, remaining holder order,
credential validity, and registration data;
else (all holders archive)
  :Credential_ArchiveAsAllHolders;
  :All current holders authorize, or anchorers if holderless;
  :Credential_ArchiveAsAnchorers is also available independently;
  :Terminate without replacement;
endif
stop

note right
The simplified lifecycle operations are:
CredentialRegistryFactory_Issue,
CredentialLifecycle_Renew, and
RegisteredCredentialLifecycle_Renew.

RegisteredCredential is registration-only and requires Credential.
RegisteredCredentialLifecycle requires RegisteredCredential,
CredentialLifecycle, and compiler-required transitive Credential.
A concrete contract may implement all four interfaces.

Payment is optional profile policy. Future payment rules
must resolve authorization, atomicity, replay, refunds,
finality, pricing, concurrency, privacy, and auditability.
end note

@enduml
